  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "StatefulSets: A Disk per Pod",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Snapshot CRDs + snapshot-controller are __add-ons__, absent on a bare cluster",
            "Trusting `spec.capacity` and declaring the resize done",
            "Expecting a shrink to work — it silently never reconciles",
            "Deleting the namespace and assuming the ==billed snapshots== died with it"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`volumeClaimTemplates` = a PVC **factory**, one claim per ordinal",
            "Deployment replicas mount the {red:same} claim — writes collide",
            "StatefulSet replicas mount {green:disjoint} claims — no collision",
            "Stable network identity **plus** stable storage identity",
            "That pair is what makes ==databases and quorum systems== work"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism: Naming",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "<template>-<statefulset>-<ordinal>",
            "data-postgres-0   # replica 0",
            "data-postgres-1   # replica 1",
            "data-postgres-2   # replica 2"
          ],
          "note": "deterministic, so reattach is exact"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "chain",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Pod to Disk",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "StatefulSet postgres",
                "note": "replicas: 3",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "Pod postgres-1",
                "note": "stable DNS name",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "PVC data-postgres-1",
                "note": "never renamed",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "PV / CSI volume",
                "note": "same disk on reschedule",
                "ink": "orange"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: 3 x 100Gi",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "volumeClaimTemplates:",
            "- metadata: {name: data}",
            "  spec:",
            "    accessModes: [ReadWriteOnce]",
            "    storageClassName: fast-ssd",
            "    resources:",
            "      requests: {storage: 100Gi}"
          ],
          "note": "3 replicas = 3 x 100Gi billed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`WaitForFirstConsumer` provisions each volume {green:where its pod lands}",
            "3 replicas spread over 3 AZs = 3 disks in 3 AZs",
            "Immediate binding instead risks a **zone mismatch** and Pending"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Retention Policy",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field",
            "Value",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "whenScaled",
              "Retain",
              "scale down keeps disks"
            ],
            [
              "whenScaled",
              "Delete",
              "scale down wipes them"
            ],
            [
              "whenDeleted",
              "Retain",
              "default, data survives"
            ],
            [
              "whenDeleted",
              "Delete",
              "PVCs go with the set"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "Grow, Copy and Restore Volumes"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Replication Layers, Restore Drills and Failure Seams",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Default is keep",
          "text": "PVCs ==survive scale-down and deletion==; scaling back up **reuses** the old data. `persistentVolumeClaimRetentionPolicy` is the opt-in to automatic cleanup."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Local persistent volumes give ==raw-disk speed== but pin the pod to one node",
            "Node loss is **data loss** unless the app replicates",
            "Pick one replication layer on purpose, not by accident"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Restore drill",
          "text": "Snapshot taken != data recoverable. Time a real restore: new PVC from `dataSource`, correct name, pod comes up healthy."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Comparison: Where to Replicate",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Layer",
            "Example",
            "Cost / risk"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "App",
              "Postgres stream, Cassandra",
              "N full copies, app-aware"
            ],
            [
              "Storage",
              "Ceph, cloud disk",
              "transparent, blind to data"
            ],
            [
              "Local PV",
              "raw NVMe",
              "fastest, {red:node = SPOF}"
            ],
            [
              "Both",
              "app + replicated disk",
              "pay **twice**, rarely needed"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Using a Deployment with one RWO PVC and scaling to 3",
            "Deleting the StatefulSet and expecting the disks gone",
            "Editing `volumeClaimTemplates` in place — the field is immutable",
            "Trusting a snapshot schedule as a **backup**",
            "Never rehearsing restore, including ==PVC recreation=="
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Storage fails at __four seams__: ==binding==, ==attach/mount==, ==ownership== and ==reclaim== — and every one of them shows up in `kubectl describe` events before it shows up in your logs.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Symptom Table",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Real cause",
            "First look"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "PVC `Pending`",
              "no PV, bad class, zone mismatch",
              "`describe pvc`"
            ],
            [
              "`Pending`, class OK",
              "provisioner pod down",
              "provisioner logs"
            ],
            [
              "`ContainerCreating`",
              "`FailedMount ... timed out`",
              "kubelet + CSI node"
            ],
            [
              "`Multi-Attach error`",
              "RWO still on old node",
              "`get volumeattachment`"
            ],
            [
              "PVC stuck `Terminating`",
              "finalizer waits on a pod",
              "find the consumer"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Node goes **NotReady**, pod reschedules, old attach survives = Multi-Attach",
            "Never force-patch a PVC finalizer — delete the __pod__ that holds it",
            "`Released` PV never rebinds until `spec.claimRef` is cleared"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "One page to revise the whole model: __objects__, __access modes__, __policies__, ==commands== and the debug order.",
          "ink": "black"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "volumeClaimTemplates, stable identity, retention"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Ownership, Ephemeral Pressure and the Storage Bill",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Ownership: fsGroup",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Fresh volumes are __root-owned__; a non-root container gets `Permission denied`. `fsGroup` makes the kubelet {green:chown} the volume to that GID at mount.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "securityContext:",
            "  runAsUser: 1000",
            "  fsGroup: 2000        # chown -R",
            "  fsGroupChangePolicy:",
            "    OnRootMismatch     # skip if ok"
          ],
          "note": "recursive chown = minutes on 1M files"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Key rule",
          "text": "Read the __events__, not the spec: `describe pvc` names the binding fault, `describe pod` names the mount fault, and the cloud bill names everything you forgot to delete."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Rescue a Released PV",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl patch pv pv-01 -p \\",
            "  '{\"spec\":{\"claimRef\":null}}'",
            "# phase: Released -> Available"
          ],
          "note": "Retain policy only; data is still there"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Ephemeral Storage Pressure",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`No space left on device`, then pods **Evicted** on `ephemeral-storage`",
            "emptyDir + container logs + image layers all bill the __node disk__",
            "Cap the pod with requests/limits; cap the scratch dir with `sizeLimit`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "resources:",
            "  limits:",
            "    ephemeral-storage: 2Gi",
            "volumes:",
            "- name: tmp",
            "  emptyDir: {sizeLimit: 500Mi}"
          ],
          "note": "one pod cannot fill the node"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Cost and Quota",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Cost trap",
            "Still billed?",
            "Sweep"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Orphaned `Retain` PVs",
              "yes",
              "`get pv` Released"
            ],
            [
              "Unused snapshots",
              "yes",
              "`get volumesnapshot`"
            ],
            [
              "Over-provisioned IOPS",
              "yes",
              "gp3 `iops` param"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "# storageClassName unset:",
            "#   -> default class",
            "storageClassName: \"\"",
            "# empty string: no dynamic",
            "#   provisioning, static only"
          ],
          "note": "unset and \"\" are NOT the same"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Stuck Terminating PVC",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`pvc-protection` finalizer holds the PVC while a __pod__ mounts it",
            "`describe pvc` lists the consumer under ==Used By==",
            "Delete or scale down the consumer — the PVC then finishes"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "volumeClaimTemplates, stable identity, retention"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Clearing Finalizers, Reclaim Defaults and Storage Quotas",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl describe pvc pgdata",
            "# Used By: web-7d9f-x2k",
            "kubectl delete pod web-7d9f-x2k",
            "# finalizer clears, PVC gone"
          ],
          "note": "never patch the finalizer away"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Delete is the default",
          "text": "Dynamic PVs inherit {red:Delete}: removing the PVC **destroys** the disk. Put `reclaimPolicy: Retain` on classes holding data you cannot rebuild."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Storage Quota",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "kind: ResourceQuota",
            "spec:",
            "  hard:",
            "    requests.storage: 500Gi",
            "    gold.storageclass.storage.",
            "    k8s.io/requests.storage: 100Gi"
          ],
          "note": "per-class cap stops silent SSD sprawl"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Quota key",
            "Caps"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`requests.storage`",
              "sum of PVC requests"
            ],
            [
              "`persistentvolumeclaims`",
              "PVC count"
            ],
            [
              "`<class>...requests.storage`",
              "one class's total"
            ],
            [
              "`<class>...persistentvolumeclaims`",
              "PVCs per class"
            ],
            [
              "`requests.ephemeral-storage`",
              "node scratch disk"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sweep ==Released== PVs monthly — they bill until deleted",
            "Delete snapshots nobody has restored from in a quarter",
            "Right-size gp3 `iops` and throughput to real usage",
            "Quota every namespace, tightest on the __fast__ class"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "volumeClaimTemplates, stable identity, retention"
    },
