          "type": "heading",
          "text": "11. Mount Gotchas",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Mounting over a non-empty dir __hides__ the original files",
            "`subPath` mounts one file — no live configMap refresh",
            "`subPathExpr` expands env vars like the pod name",
            "`volumeMode: Block` = raw device at `volumeDevices`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "12. Stable Names",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "data-postgres-0",
            "data-postgres-1",
            "# <template>-<sts>-<ordinal>"
          ],
          "note": "rescheduled pod reattaches same disk"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "13. Binding Facts",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Rule",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "One PVC ↔ one PV",
              "exclusive, never split"
            ],
            [
              "PVC 10Gi on 50Gi PV",
              "binds, **40Gi wasted**"
            ],
            [
              "`volumeName` set",
              "forces that exact PV"
            ],
            [
              "`selector` labels",
              "static pool matching"
            ],
            [
              "`pvc-protection`",
              "in-use PVC only `Terminating`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "14. PV Phases",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Phase",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Available",
              "free, waiting for a claim"
            ],
            [
              "Bound",
              "held by one PVC"
            ],
            [
              "{red:Released}",
              "PVC gone, data __not__ reclaimed"
            ],
            [
              "Failed",
              "reclaim itself errored"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "15. Expansion Rules",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Class must set ==allowVolumeExpansion: true==",
            "Two stages: ControllerExpand then **NodeExpand** (filesystem)",
            "Watch `status.capacity`, never `spec` — spec lies early",
            "Old drivers need a pod restart to finish the resize",
            "Shrink is **never** supported — new volume + copy"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "16. Snapshot Truths",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Snapshots are ==crash-consistent==, not application-consistent",
            "Quiesce, or use the DB's own backup, for a transactional copy",
            "Clone `dataSource` = same __class__ and same __namespace__ only",
            "Snapshots live in the **backend** — deleting the namespace still bills"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "17. Class Gotchas",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "metadata:",
            "  annotations:",
            "    storageclass.kubernetes.io/",
            "    is-default-class: \"true\""
          ],
          "note": "two defaults or none = Pending claims"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Classes are effectively __immutable__ — make a new one and migrate",
            "Reclaim is inherited at provision time; default is {red:Delete}",
            "Tier by name (`fast-ssd`, `standard`, `cheap-cold`), not by backend"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
